## Author of Latest Modifications (`cmix-neif-3.1`)

* **Copyright (C) 2026 Oleksandr Dreval**
  * GitHub Profile: <https://github.com/OleksandrDreval>
  * Project Repository: <https://github.com/OleksandrDreval/cmix-neif-3.1>
  * Scope of copyright & GPL-3.0 section 5a modifications (November 2026):
    1. Stage-2 self-extracting stub `systrap` warm-up fix, stage-1 bootstrap
       context-mixer re-tuning, and single-pass forward `cm_compress_k` (`K = a.outn + 4`
       at `i == nd`) packer build (`1.51 GiB` peak RSS, `~39.0 s`, zero unpacker or
       decompressor executions) (`tools_src/packer/stub.c`, `tools_src/packer/boot_models.h`,
       `tools_src/packer/cm_core.h`, `tools_src/packer/pack_tool.c`,
       `tools_src/packer/build_packer.sh`, `build_and_construct_comp.sh`).
    2. Lossless `.c5` transformer weight container entropy-coding upgrades
       (Sign-Magnitude `ENC_INT4W`, per-canonical-name probability tables,
       16-bucket node-aware width context `b`, 4-way integer probability mixing
       (`>> 5`) at each `ENC_INT4W` binary tree node combining `p_tree`,
       2D spatial context `p_2d` with RoPE parity `k & 1`, 3D spatial context
       `p_3d`, and Bayesian row-column posterior `p_rc` on a stride-4 2-bit
       magnitude tree with 100 % Stream A `{0, ±2, ±4, ±7}` grid coverage,
       eliminating per-row `gbit` flags and saving `~408 KiB` in `ModelleId`;
       4-way integer probability mixing for `ENC_INT4W` signs combining
       `sign_int4w`, `sign_2d`, `sign_rc`, and continuous magnitude-weighted
       positive-dipole posterior `p_src` with full Lehmer Stream-B absorption
       `tailB = 0 B`; pre-snap 4-bit mantissa quantization (`(val + 8) & 0xFFF0`)
       and 4-bit `lo`-nibble shift-tree coding for Stream A `ENC_BF16C` and
       non-key `ENC_F32HC` tensors with order-1 `prev_hi` `CountNode` tree
       mixing and per-`ci` + row-$L_2$-energy-bucket / column-bucket + shared
       low-nibble shift-tree mixing; header byte-role mixing `cm_role[8 * 256]`,
       adaptive order-2/1/0 `cname` character tree mixing, per-`ci`
       `prev_z`-conditioned zero-row `zr_ctx[kNamenN * 2]` mixing; empirical
       QAT bimodal sparsity priors in `FrischInt4`, cross-tensor warm-start priors
       `CopyWarmCN`, Bayesian column pseudocount `pr_c = 40`, two-stage `bfloat16`
       lo-byte adaptation shifts, `last_zrow` skipping of zero scales and dead KDA
       `key_convolution.weight` rows, and coupled `mlp.up`/`mlp.down` (`blocks.0..15`
       with full 16-block Lehmer re-permutation), KDA gate (`forget_gate_projection`,
       `output_gate_projection`), `attention.{query,key,value,output}_projection`
       (`blocks.0..15`), and `embedding.*` / `value_embeddings.0..3` /
       `prior_embedding` `{0, ±2, ±4, ±7}` QAT snapping `qat-snap` with
       feature-Gram $G_{\text{up}}$ coordinate descent and closed-form analytical
       $\text{ReLU}^2$/linear cross-covariance compensation) and re-encoded
       `3,043,805 B` container `weights-poc8m_w2048_tf2t3_pruned_v5k_np2.c5`
       (`src/tf1/`, `src/transformer.h`,
       `training/tf/3_train/export/np2/tf1_np_codec.cpp`).
    3. `BITLSTM` slot-1 3-bit mantissa rounding, single-byte `(e_code << 4) | s`
       `kBlobW[24669]` packing (`-24,489 B` `.rodata`, `-49.8 %`) with 90-byte
       exception tail (`kSlotExcOff[3] = {0, 4, 55}`), active-cell `H = kSlotH[slot]`
       (`H = 16` via `Dot16Preloaded` for slot 0, `H = 32` via `Dot32Preloaded`
       for slots 1 and 2) 100 % IEEE-754 bit-exact frozen AVX2 inference fast-path
       with transposed non-FMA `hidP` projection and pruning of 39 dead training
       fields from `struct Head` (`src/bit_head_weights.h`, `src/bit_head.cpp`),
       plus AVX2 column-scaling in `mixer_precond.cpp`, dead-code pruning
       (`sse.cpp`, `glibc_compat.cpp`, `ppmd_page.{h,cpp}`), and `COLD_SIZE_ATTR`
       layout.
    4. ~2.86x peak RAM reduction across the `PPMd` page pool (`zonen_textrahmen`
       `4 MiB` rounding fix, removal of phantom `+2.12 GiB` `ppmd_page::raum`
       pre-accounting, demand-paged `memfd`), single-mapping demand-paged
       `SEMCACHE` (`MAP_NORESERVE` + `FreeFxcmRest` `munmap` with exact
       `kNLog = 24, kB = 18` SimHash geometry), `word_label` 69 MiB leak fix in
       `FreeFxcmRest()` and `PAGE_REGISTRY_ADD` dangling-pointer removal,
       decompressor/postprocessor memory-safety & `~161 MiB` peak heap reduction
       (`article_reorder.h`, `komm_transform.h`, `page_form.h`,
       `phda9_preprocess.h`, `cmtidx_transform.h`, `census_transform.h`,
       `preprocessor.cpp`, `runner.cpp`, `misc.h` vectorized `memchr`/`memmem`
       I/O), and 4 KiB demand-paged `arena` / `HugeBuf` allocators, plus 4-row
       AVX2 unrolling in `SemDotPm1` (`src/models/ppmd*.{h,cpp}`,
       `src/semantic_cache.h`, `src/predictor.cpp`, `src/word_label.cpp`,
       `src/runner.cpp`, `src/arena_alloc.h`, `src/tf1/opt/arena_build.cpp`).
    5. Compiler warning cleanups and PGO diagnostic flags across `src/` and
       `makefile`, plus analytical/benchmark documentation
       (`en-optimization_report_it_1.md`..`en-optimization_report_it_6.md`,
       `uk-optimization_report_it_1.md`..`uk-optimization_report_it_6.md`,
       `CHANGES.md`, `NOTICE.md`, `README.md`, `training/`).

No copyright claim is made by Oleksandr Dreval over inherited upstream code;
his copyright claim covers the `cmix-neif-3.1` modifications and reports only,
licensed under `GPL-3.0-only`.

